An old man leans on a hoe he plainly never uses, smiling the warm smile of someone about to do you a kindness you'll regret.
"You're Ona's, then. Carrying her little seed the long way round. Bless her. Bless the both of you."
"I've a faster road. A small mutation, kindly meant — make it stronger, so it lives longer. That's all. That's all it ever is."
[The hoe shifts. Under the warmth there is the Revel's hunger, wearing a grandfather's face.]
"The trait comes up the long way pale and true. My way it comes up brighter. Wrong-bright. But who's counting petals when the thing is strong?"
"Ona counts. Ona always counts."
[You turn the seed over once, and put Garran's smile behind you. The long way, then. The true way.]
"Pity. Honest pity. You'll do well here, and slowly — which the Glut respects, and I never could."
